# Build context of the frontend image (docker build -f Dockerfile.frontend .), which is also what
# Compose uses for it. Dockerfile.frontend copies only the package files, public/, src/index.jsx,
# src/frontend/ and docker/nginx.conf, so everything else stays out of the context: it is faster,
# and local secrets (.env files) can never reach the build.
.git
.github
.claude
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
build
coverage
**/coverage
playwright-report
playwright-results
test-results
e2e
docs
scripts
src/backend
*.md
